{"id":"g07","name":"Prepare Driver Classification Data","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","train_df","test_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The taxi company prepares its driver data for a classifier. You get <code>train_df</code> and <code>test_df</code> with the same columns: <code>driver_id</code> int, <code>car_model</code> string, <code>car_manufacture_year</code> int, <code>days_since_inspection</code> int, <code>age</code> int (can be null), <code>experience</code> int, <code>second_language</code> string, <code>rating</code> double, <code>net_worth_of_tips</code> double, <code>number_of_rejected_rides</code>, <code>number_of_upvotes</code>, <code>number_of_complaints</code>, <code>number_of_incidents</code> (int), and <code>driver_class</code> string (can be null in the test data).</p>\n<p>Every statistic below is computed on the <b>training data only</b>, then applied to both tables:</p>\n<ol><li><code>age</code>: replace null ages with the mean of the non-null training ages, then truncate every age to an integer (drop the decimals).</li>\n<li><code>car_model</code> and <code>second_language</code>: sort the distinct training values in ascending order and replace each value by its position <code>0, 1, 2, ...</code> in that list. A value never seen in the training data becomes <code>-1</code>.</li>\n<li><code>net_worth_of_tips</code>: replace each value by <code>(value - mean) / std</code>, where mean and std are the training mean and <b>population</b> standard deviation (divide by N), rounded to 5 decimal places. If that std is <code>0</code>, the standardized value is <code>0</code>.</li>\n<li><code>driver_class</code>: <code>\"A class\"</code> becomes <code>0</code>, <code>\"B class\"</code> becomes <code>1</code>, null stays null.</li></ol>\n<p>All other columns are unchanged. Return one DataFrame whose first column is <code>dataset</code> (<code>\"train\"</code> or <code>\"test\"</code>), followed by the 14 columns above in the same order, with all training rows first, then all test rows, each group sorted by <code>driver_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>train_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>driver_id</th><th>car_model</th><th>car_manufacture_year</th><th>days_since_inspection</th><th>age</th><th>experience</th><th>second_language</th><th>rating</th><th>net_worth_of_tips</th><th>number_of_rejected_rides</th><th>number_of_upvotes</th><th>number_of_complaints</th><th>number_of_incidents</th><th>driver_class</th></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Toyota Prius</td><td>2018</td><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>8</td><td>French</td><td>4.6</td><td>100.0</td><td>1</td><td>12</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>A class</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Dacia Logan</td><td>2014</td><td>105</td><td>null</td><td>3</td><td>no</td><td>3.9</td><td>300.0</td><td>4</td><td>5</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>B class</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Toyota Prius</td><td>2020</td><td>0</td><td>41</td><td>22</td><td>English</td><td>4.9</td><td>200.0</td><td>0</td><td>20</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>A class</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Skoda Octavia</td><td>2019</td><td>12</td><td>26</td><td>2</td><td>no</td><td>4.1</td><td>400.0</td><td>2</td><td>9</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>B class</td></tr></table></div><p><code>test_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>driver_id</th><th>car_model</th><th>car_manufacture_year</th><th>days_since_inspection</th><th>age</th><th>experience</th><th>second_language</th><th>rating</th><th>net_worth_of_tips</th><th>number_of_rejected_rides</th><th>number_of_upvotes</th><th>number_of_complaints</th><th>number_of_incidents</th><th>driver_class</th></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Kia Niro</td><td>2021</td><td>3</td><td>null</td><td>1</td><td>Arabic</td><td>4.4</td><td>250.0</td><td>0</td><td>3</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Dacia Logan</td><td>2012</td><td>200</td><td>58</td><td>30</td><td>French</td><td>3.7</td><td>50.0</td><td>6</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>B class</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>dataset</th><th>driver_id</th><th>car_model</th><th>car_manufacture_year</th><th>days_since_inspection</th><th>age</th><th>experience</th><th>second_language</th><th>rating</th><th>net_worth_of_tips</th><th>number_of_rejected_rides</th><th>number_of_upvotes</th><th>number_of_complaints</th><th>number_of_incidents</th><th>driver_class</th></tr><tr><td>train</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>2014</td><td>105</td><td>32</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>3.9</td><td>0.44721</td><td>4</td><td>5</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>train</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>2020</td><td>0</td><td>41</td><td>22</td><td>0</td><td>4.9</td><td>-0.44721</td><td>0</td><td>20</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>train</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>2018</td><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>8</td><td>1</td><td>4.6</td><td>-1.34164</td><td>1</td><td>12</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>train</td><td>5</td><td>1</td><td>2019</td><td>12</td><td>26</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>4.1</td><td>1.34164</td><td>2</td><td>9</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>test</td><td>7</td><td>0</td><td>2012</td><td>200</td><td>58</td><td>30</td><td>1</td><td>3.7</td><td>-1.78885</td><td>6</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>test</td><td>9</td><td>-1</td><td>2021</td><td>3</td><td>32</td><td>1</td><td>-1</td><td>4.4</td><td>0.0</td><td>0</td><td>3</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>null</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB<br><b>[input]</b> DataFrame train_df, test_df</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, train_df: DataFrame, test_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return train_df\n","hints":["Calcule d'abord sur train_df seul : moyenne des âges non nuls, moyenne et écart type de population (F.stddev_pop) de net_worth_of_tips, et la liste triée des valeurs distinctes de car_model et second_language. Récupère-les avec collect().","Applique la même fonction aux deux tables, ajoute la colonne dataset, puis unionByName et trie par (train d'abord, puis driver_id). Pour l'encodage : F.create_map, ou une jointure avec une petite table valeur -> code, puis coalesce(code, -1)."],"summary_fr":"Préparer train et test pour un modèle avec des statistiques calculées sur le train SEULEMENT : remplir les âges manquants, encoder les textes en entiers, standardiser les pourboires, coder la classe en 0/1, puis renvoyer une seule table (train puis test).","tags":["statistiques du train seulement","encodage","standardisation","valeurs manquantes","union","BCG"],"minutes":30,"source":"Question rapportée du test BCG (fastprep.io, à l'origine en Pandas), réécrite en PySpark et testée par Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>solution.py</code>.</li><li>Complète la fonction <code>solve(spark, train_df, test_df)</code>. Garde son nom et ses paramètres : ce sont les tests qui l'appellent, avec leurs propres données. N'écris pas d'appel à la fonction toi-même.</li><li><code>spark</code> est une SparkSession déjà prête : ne crée pas la tienne.</li><li><code>train_df</code>, <code>test_df</code> sont des DataFrames déjà chargés : ses colonnes sont celles de l'énoncé (onglet <b>Input</b> d'un test pour les voir).</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Ta fonction doit <b>renvoyer</b> le résultat avec <code>return</code>. Un <code>print</code> ou un <code>show()</code> ne compte pas : il sort seulement dans l'onglet <b>Console Output</b>.</li><li>Le DataFrame renvoyé doit avoir <b>exactement 15 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>dataset</code>, <code>driver_id</code>, <code>car_model</code>, <code>car_manufacture_year</code>, <code>days_since_inspection</code>, <code>age</code>, <code>experience</code>, <code>second_language</code>, <code>rating</code>, <code>net_worth_of_tips</code>, <code>number_of_rejected_rides</code>, <code>number_of_upvotes</code>, <code>number_of_complaints</code>, <code>number_of_incidents</code>, <code>driver_class</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Finis par un <code>select(...)</code> de ces colonnes.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>orderBy</code> à la fin).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Spark tourne dans ton Codespace : au premier RUN TESTS de la séance, attends qu'il soit prêt (1 à 2 minutes). Ensuite chaque lancement prend quelques secondes.</li><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 5 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"train_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"driver_id int, car_model string, car_manufacture_year int, days_since_inspection int, age int, experience int, second_language string, rating double, net_worth_of_tips double, number_of_rejected_rides int, number_of_upvotes int, number_of_complaints int, number_of_incidents int, driver_class string","rows":[[3,"Toyota Prius",2018,31,30,8,"French",4.6,100.0,1,12,0,0,"A class"],[1,"Dacia Logan",2014,105,null,3,"no",3.9,300.0,4,5,2,1,"B class"],[2,"Toyota Prius",2020,0,41,22,"English",4.9,200.0,0,20,0,0,"A class"],[5,"Skoda Octavia",2019,12,26,2,"no",4.1,400.0,2,9,1,0,"B class"]]}},"test_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"driver_id int, car_model string, car_manufacture_year int, days_since_inspection int, age int, experience int, second_language string, rating double, net_worth_of_tips double, number_of_rejected_rides int, number_of_upvotes int, number_of_complaints int, number_of_incidents int, driver_class string","rows":[[9,"Kia Niro",2021,3,null,1,"Arabic",4.4,250.0,0,3,0,0,null],[7,"Dacia Logan",2012,200,58,30,"French",3.7,50.0,6,2,3,2,"B class"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["dataset","driver_id","car_model","car_manufacture_year","days_since_inspection","age","experience","second_language","rating","net_worth_of_tips","number_of_rejected_rides","number_of_upvotes","number_of_complaints","number_of_incidents","driver_class"],"rows":[["train",1,0,2014,105,32,3,2,3.9,0.44721,4,5,2,1,1],["train",2,2,2020,0,41,22,0,4.9,-0.44721,0,20,0,0,0],["train",3,2,2018,31,30,8,1,4.6,-1.34164,1,12,0,0,0],["train",5,1,2019,12,26,2,2,4.1,1.34164,2,9,1,0,1],["test",7,0,2012,200,58,30,1,3.7,-1.78885,6,2,3,2,1],["test",9,-1,2021,3,32,1,-1,4.4,0.0,0,3,0,0,null]]}},{"input":{"train_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"driver_id int, car_model string, car_manufacture_year int, days_since_inspection int, age int, experience int, second_language string, rating double, net_worth_of_tips double, number_of_rejected_rides int, number_of_upvotes int, number_of_complaints int, number_of_incidents int, driver_class string","rows":[[1,"Kia Niro",2020,10,33,5,"no",4.0,80.0,0,4,0,0,"A class"],[2,"Kia Niro",2021,20,34,6,"no",4.2,80.0,1,5,0,0,"B class"]]}},"test_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"driver_id int, car_model string, car_manufacture_year int, days_since_inspection int, age int, experience int, second_language string, rating do